course: dictionary
lesson: 15109
title: Words from church life
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Some words belong to a special place, such as a church. «Sacramental» is one of them. It comes from sacrament, a holy rite such as baptism or communion. The ending -al means connected with, so sacramental means connected with a holy rite.
explain: As an adjective, sacramental describes a thing. «The priest blessed the sacramental bread.» The bread is not for a sandwich. It is used in a holy rite, so sacramental tells you what kind of bread it is.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «They shared the sacramental wine at the service.» Shared at a service and used in a holy act tell you this is church ritual. Swap in holy or sacred: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Sacramental means connected with a sacrament, a holy rite such as baptism or communion.
fact: As an adjective, sacramental describes things, such as «sacramental wine» or «sacramental bread».
fact: As a noun, a sacramental is a blessed object or action, such as holy water or a rosary, which Catholics believe helps their prayer.
fact: «The sacramental life» means the holy rites and church life of a church community.
fact: Sacramental can also mean feeling holy or very special, as in «a sacramental hush in the chapel».
exercise: «The priest blessed the sacramental bread.» What does sacramental mean here? | Made of sugar | Very cheap | *Connected with a holy rite | Brown in colour
exercise: Catholics keep sacramentals at home. Which of these is a sacramental? | *A rosary | A football | A library book | A bicycle
exercise: «In the sacramental life of the church, families come together for prayer.» What does sacramental suggest? | Cooking and baking | Shopping and sport | Homework and reading | *Holy rites and church sacraments
test: «They shared the sacramental wine at communion.» What does sacramental mean? | Cheap and plain | *Connected with a holy rite | Sour and cold | Very loud
test: A blessed object, such as holy water, is called what? | A tennis ball | A library card | A pencil case | *A sacramental
exam: «The old chapel felt sacramental in the quiet candlelight.» What does sacramental mean here? | Cold and wet | Noisy and busy | *Feeling holy or very special | Made of plastic
